SEAM-25: step 4, before-and-after pictures of the six counties at the device's views, and a seam count. Registered
before any code for it (map-server, 2026-11-15). The pictures go to the owner unopened, before anything ships. Host only:
no board, no network. Every input is read-only. Nothing touches the held cache except reading the county file.
Heavy steps (store build, package builds) run only outside the owner's sitting (17:30-20:50Z).

S4-0 THE REGION-BOX HYPOTHESIS, as a count, before any picture.
- What is tested: each county's region box is its 2024 county polygon's bounding box (ingest-basemap.ts:436-440 at 6a11b5a21d0a,
  tl_2024_us_county.zip). A square reads a county's file only when it meets that box. So a 2025 feature reaching outside
  its county's 2024 box can be missed by a square that meets the feature but not the box: one seam mechanism.
- The count, per 2025 file: features; features with any vertex outside the county's 2024 box; the largest overshoot, in
  whole metres. No coordinate is printed. The county file is read from the held cache, read-only, with its mtime checked.
- Predicted: 0 features outside the box, in all six.
- Outside: any > 0 -> the hypothesis is LIVE for that county. Report the counts, and that county gets one extra centre at
  its largest overshoot (S4-1's rule 2).

S4-1 THE CENTRES, one per county by rule 1 (plus rule 2's, if S4-0 found any). Computed by a script, printed at 2 dp, and
FROZEN in an addendum to this file BEFORE any package is built.
- Rule 1: the point on the county's line with a 2024 neighbour that is nearest the county's largest 2025 feature touching
  that line within 100 m. Largest is by AWATER for water, by length for rivers. If no feature touches the line, the
  boundary point nearest the largest feature.
- Rule 2: the overshoot's point, if S4-0 found one.
- 2 dp is about 1 km, which is <= 5 px at 10 mi. Public geography: county lines.

S4-2 THE PACKAGES AND THE PICTURES. One package per centre and side, requested as the device's MapQuery asks (MapQuery.h), rendered at
10 / 25 / 50 mi by the device's own maplayer::Build on the host (the sibling's headers, fb_counts.cpp's view), dark theme,
weather off.
- BEFORE: main's builder (b282699ac091) over the served store 4c0875738f38 (scratchpad/bm-obj, read-only).
- AFTER: #696's builder (6a11b5a21d0a, or the head as it then stands) over the new store from step 8's dry run.
- THE NAMED CONFOUND: AFTER differs from BEFORE by the six's data AND by #696's builder (the ladder, D2, the sea layer the
  served store does not have). A difference away from the six's lines is expected and is not a seam. The seam count reads
  AFTER alone.
- Per centre and rung: BEFORE.png, AFTER.png, and SEAM.png (AFTER, with the county line and any seam pixel marked).

S4-3 THE SEAM: definition, finder, and control.
- Definition: on the county line L between a 2025 county and a 2024 neighbour (L from the 2024 county file, projected with
  the same view), inside the disc, a SEAM PIXEL is a pixel within 1 px of L that is land, while the pixels 2 and 3 px from L
  on BOTH sides, along L's normal, are water or river (a land gap through water at L).
- Finder: sample L every 0.5 px inside the disc; count seam pixels and samples per picture. Printed as counts only.
- Predicted: 0 seam pixels in every AFTER picture.
- CONTROL, the planted offset: a COPY of one AFTER package (the 44007 centre: the largest file). Every water ring whose
  centroid lies inside 44007's 2024 polygon is shifted 500 m east (about 3.7 px at 10 mi), re-encoded, and rendered.
  Predicted: > 0 seam pixels at 10 mi on that centre's line. Graded at 10 mi only: at 50 mi, 500 m is under 1 px.
  The plant is only in the copy, and is proved applied by a changed package sha before it is read.
- OUTSIDE THE SET:
  - the control reading 0 at 10 mi -> the finder is blind; no seam reading is given.
  - any AFTER seam pixel > 0 -> that picture and its counts go to the owner with the rest, flagged; nothing ships without
    his ruling.
  - a package not building -> STOP and report.
  - anything else -> stop and decide.

S4-4 TO THE OWNER, unopened by map-server, through the orchestrator:
- the pictures;
- S4-0's counts and S4-3's counts;
- the control's reading;
- the confound sentence above;
- the six sizes, and 39167's 5.5% as the one file whose size moved.
FROZEN 2026-11-15T16:29:17Z

AMENDMENT 1, S4-3b (the orchestrator's addition, accepted with SEAM-25): the other vintage seam, a break.
- A BREAK PIXEL: a water or river pixel within 1 px of L, whose mirror across L along the normal, at 1, 2 and 3 px, holds no
  water or river at any of the three. Water meets land across the line. Counted per picture, in BEFORE and in AFTER, by the
  same finder (L sampled every 0.5 px inside the disc). Printed as counts only.
- Predicted, BEFORE: > 0 at most centres. On unchanged data, an oblique river crossing or a shore that meets L makes break
  pixels by geometry alone, so S4-3b is read COMPARATIVELY, never as an absolute.
- Predicted, AFTER against BEFORE at the same centre and rung: |AFTER - BEFORE| <= T, T = max(4, ceil(0.25 x BEFORE)), at
  every centre and rung.
- The confound, named again: AFTER also carries #696's builder, whose ladder and D2 move shoreline pixels near L. So a count
  outside T is FLAGGED to the owner with its three pictures, as "AFTER breaks more (or fewer) than BEFORE here". It is not
  called a seam without the picture.
- CONTROL: a COPY of the 17005 AFTER package (rivers), where every river polyline with a vertex inside 17005's 2024 polygon is
  shifted 500 m along L (L's direction at the centre).
  - Predicted: S4-3b at 10 mi rises by >= 2 over the unshifted AFTER.
  - The plant is proved by a changed package sha before it is read.
  - If it does not rise, S4-3b is blind and no S4-3b reading is given.
AMENDED 2026-11-15T16:48:51Z

AMENDMENT 2, S4-0's instrument checks, added before S4-0 runs (tool mirror/s40_box.py). These are not predictions; either
failing means the instrument is unreliable, and NO S4-0 reading is given.
- A, the anchor: the cached 2024 neighbour tl_2024_38045_areawater reads 0 features outside its own 2024 county box. 2024
  water is clipped to 2024 county lines, so a correct reader cannot find any outside.
- B, the plant: with every county box shrunk 100 m on each side, at least one of the six files reads > 0 outside. This proves
  the comparison can fire.
- The box is computed as the code computes it (ingest-basemap.ts:431-434): the exact bbox of the 2024 polygon's vertices, with
  no padding.
- An off reading of S4-0 itself STOPS, and goes to the orchestrator before anything else is done.
AMENDED 2026-11-15T16:50:06Z

